SUMMARY:Carnival of Falatados
LOCATION:Falatados\, Tinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On the last Sunday of Carnival the big village of Falatados stages a themed parade with satirical floats\, traditional instruments and a raki-fuelled street party\, the largest carnival on Tinos. Nearby Agapi does the 'Makaronas' straw-effigy procession ending in a communal pasta meal\, and Triantaros reads out satirical verses on Carnival Thursday.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/tinos/#falatados-carnival-of-falatados
